-- ex39 registered capabilities: matrix algebra, graph dispatch, and behavior dispatch. Twin of 071-tier3-opaque.bqn.
-- Formal witness: native matrix algebra and host dispatch are registered capabilities, not tiers.
-- Graph and behavior carriers expose host callables rather than native array operations. The matrix interface stays native algebra; capabilities and signatures decide which operations exist.
-- Adj is registered as a set-valued fiber-matrix: fiber i holds row i's BITS, so the matrix view's row fold +/ Adj@row is the out-degree 2 1 3 0 2 (node 3's all-zero row folds to the identity 0).
-- shortestPath and runBehaviorTree pass selected rows and registered payloads to host functions. Those calls write nothing here. The expects show BTree unchanged and OutDeg preserved after dispatch.
-- Left to the .bqn twin: env ≡ 1 3 4 and /cursor ≡ ⟨3⟩ (the envelopes are exactly the hostile/cursor fixtures, definitional), adj bit-identity (a set-valued column has no expect form), and the "patrol" payload gather (BQN-internal).
--! registry ../registries/071-tier3-opaque.reg
--! expect outDeg = 2 1 3 0 2
--! expect btree = seek flee guard patrol idle

Node , OutDeg = +/ Adj@row
Hostile , shortestPath via Adj
^cursor , runBehaviorTree
